ut":{"what":"Vertex Pharmaceuticals (VRTX). This chart runs from May 1, 2017 to Sep 6, 2017.","setup":"The stock rose about 54% in the three months before the base. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $137.26 and pulling back 9% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jul 19, 2017 it closed at $159.69, its first close above the base high of $137.26. Volume that day was 16.8M shares, 11.21x the prior 10-day average of 1.5M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $166.11, and the chart ends at $157.08.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}